    "body": "> So we're all aligned that the spec as-is will not run defer scripts in the same task, and between the execution of two defer scripts we fully defer to the event loop which may run other queued tasks and indeed update the rendering?\r\n\r\nYes! Though [rendering opportunity](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#rendering-opportunity) is implementation-specific and mentions \"user agent throttling for performance reasons\". Throttling rendering due to having pending scripts would be per-spec.",
